  "rule": [
    "Canonical text follows Python json.dumps(value, sort_keys=True, separators=(',', ':'), ensure_ascii=False, allow_nan=False).",
    "Object keys sort by Unicode code point sequence (Python str ordering), not by locale or UTF-16 code unit.",
    "Numbers must be finite. Integers must satisfy |n| <= 2^53. A float whose value is integral and |v| <= 2^53 is emitted as an integer (1.0 -> 1, -0.0 -> 0).",
    "Other floats use Python repr(float): shortest round-trip digits; exponent form when decimal exponent < -4 or >= 16; exponent has explicit sign and at least two digits (1e-07, 1.5e+16).",
    "Strings escape only \\\" \\\\ and control characters U+0000-U+001F (\\n \\r \\t \\b \\f, otherwise \\u00XX lowercase hex). Non-ASCII, U+007F and U+2028 stay raw. Lone surrogates are rejected.",
    "Digest is sha256 hex of the UTF-8 bytes of the canonical text."
  ],
